    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 803,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Amazonas (Venezuelan state)\nAmazonas State ( Estado Amazonas , [ es\u02c8ta\u00f0o ama\u02c8sonas ] ) is one of the 23 states ( estados ) into which Venezuela is divided . It covers nearly a fifth of the area of Venezuela , but has less than 1 % of Venezuela 's total population . The state capital is Puerto Ayacucho . The capital until the early 1900s was San Fernando de Atabapo . Although named after the Amazon River , most of the state is drained by the Orinoco River . Amazonas State covers a total surface area of 176,899 km \u00b2 and , in 2007 , had a population of 142,200 . Its density is of 0.8 inhabitants per km \u00b2 . Amazonas has Venezuela 's highest proportion of indigenous peoples of Venezuela ; these make up only around 1.5 % of the population nationwide , but the proportion is nearly 50 % in Amazonas ."
     }
